  "story": {
    "language": "en",
    "translationLanguage": "zh-Hant",
    "textEn": "At the library, I want to borrow an interesting story about a child and a dog. The shelf is tall, so I search on the computer before I choose a book. A helpful woman shows me where to look on the screen, and I check the picture on the cover. My friend carries a heavy pile of books past the desk, while another person comes to return a book. I find a place at the table and pull my chair closer to the window. Then I read the first page and point to a picture of the dog running beside its friend. The room is quiet, and I keep my bag off the floor so other people can walk past. I want to know what happens next, so I take my book to the desk. After the book is checked, I put it in my bag and promise to bring it back next week.",
    "textZh": "在圖書館，我想借一本關於孩子和狗的有趣故事。書架很高，所以挑書前，我先用電腦搜尋。一位樂於助人的女士指給我看螢幕上該找哪裡，我也看看封面上的圖畫。朋友抱著一大疊很重的書經過服務台，另一位讀者則來還書。我在桌邊找個位置，把椅子拉到比較靠近窗戶的地方。接著我讀第一頁，指著一張狗在朋友旁邊跑步的圖畫。室內很安靜，我讓袋子不占用地板，讓其他人可以走過。我想知道接下來發生什麼，所以把書拿到服務台。借閱手續完成後，我把書放進袋子，答應下週帶回來。",
